# Fork-local voice backstop. MUST stay untracked: update-system.mjs apply only
# touches its allowlist and never sweeps unknown files, so "untracked + unlisted"
# is the entire preservation mechanism (same trick as redline-check.mjs). Tracking
# either of these also trips validate-system-paths-coverage.mjs as an orphan, and
# a tracked tests/ file gets pruned by the updater on the first apply.
bk-voice-lint.mjs
tests/bk-voice-lint.test.mjs
output/.voice-lint/
# Same reasoning: tests/ is on SYSTEM_PATHS and the updater prunes any TRACKED
# tests/ file absent from upstream, so this must stay untracked to survive.
tests/cover-letter-prose.test.mjs

# The rest of the fork-owned PDF/cover-letter chain, untracked for the same
# reason — and these were NOT safe before, they were only lucky.
#
# apply() PRESERVES a locally-modified system file, but preservation is ONE-SHOT:
# the preserved file is held out of the update COMMIT by an :(exclude) pathspec,
# so at the NEXT update it is byte-identical to the new baseline, drops out of
# `atRisk = changedLocally ∩ differsFromUpstream`, and — being absent upstream —
# gets pruned. The cycle is: pruned → restored by hand → now differs → preserved
# → frozen → baseline resets → exposed → pruned again. These five were pruned at
# v1.29.0, restored, preserved through v1.30.0, and `node fork-check.mjs` showed
# them back in the exposed state for v1.31.0. Untracking breaks the cycle: the
# prune spares untracked files unconditionally.
#
# v1.30.0's isReferencedByPreservedFile() does NOT rescue them — it only scans
# preserved .html/.css for a basename, and the prose template is reached from a
# .mjs. Nor does config/local-paths.txt: localUserPaths() rejects any path that
# collides with a SYSTEM_PATHS entry, and templates/ and tests/ are both on it.
# Untracked is the only mechanism left.
templates/cover-letter-prose-template.html
tests/pdf-content-check.test.mjs
tests/fixtures/pdf-flow-fixture.html
tests/fixtures/pdf-footer-fixture.html
tests/fixtures/pdf-rtl-fixture.html

# Two scanner providers upstream has REMOVED but portals.yml still routes to:
# `provider: macher` and `provider: jobsgemach` in tracked_companies. Both are
# absent from upstream and were therefore prune-bait; jobsgemach.mjs was in fact
# deleted by the v1.30.0 apply on 2026-08-27 and restored from d8c98a8f^.
# providers/_registry.mjs loads this directory by readdirSync, so a missing file
# is not an import error anywhere — the provider just silently stops existing and
# that portal quietly stops being scanned. Untracked is what keeps them.
#
# Careful: a plain repo-wide grep does NOT show these as "referenced". portals.yml
# is user-layer and gitignored, so gitignore-respecting search tools skip it, and
# both providers read as dead orphans. They are not. Check portals.yml explicitly
# before concluding any provider is unused.
providers/macher.mjs
providers/jobsgemach.mjs

# test-all.mjs copies the whole repo (including cv.md, article-digest.md,
# voice-dna.md) into these scratch dirs and deletes them in a finally block. On
# Windows that rm can fail with EPERM, stranding a full copy of the user layer in
# an untracked, previously un-ignored directory — exactly what the no-user-data
# CI check exists to stop. Ignore them so a stranded copy can never be committed.
.tmp-script-test-*/

# Portfolio sources and outreach drafts. These are client-project and third-party
# detail, and `origin` is a PUBLIC fork — .github/workflows/no-user-data.yml does
# NOT cover portfolio-src/, so nothing upstream would have caught these. They were
# untracked but un-ignored (i.e. one `git add -A` from publication) until 2026-07-29.
portfolio-src/
recruiter-outreach.md

# Fork-local personal scripts. Same preservation mechanism as bk-voice-lint.mjs
# above: untracked + absent from update-system.mjs's SYSTEM_PATHS allowlist is the
# whole reason `apply` leaves them alone. Tracking any of them would also trip
# validate-system-paths-coverage.mjs as an orphan and fail test-all.mjs. Note
# merge-portfolio-pdfs.mjs additionally hardcodes a local absolute path.
export-portfolio-pdfs.mjs
export-vault-portfolio.mjs
merge-application-pdf.mjs
merge-portfolio-pdfs.mjs

# Fork-local Upwork proposal mode. The `bk-` prefix is deliberate: update-system.mjs
# merges its local SYSTEM_PATHS with a remoteSystemPaths list parsed from the REMOTE
# updater, so a plain `modes/upwork.md` would be checked out over the day upstream
# ships that name. A fork-local name upstream would never pick is the whole defence.
modes/bk-upwork.md

# Agent worktree scratch. Full repo checkouts left behind by subagent isolation;
# tracked files only, but there is no reason for them to ever be staged.
.claude/worktrees/

# Codex CLI local config. config.toml carries a plaintext MCP API key in
# [mcp_servers.*.env], and `origin` is a PUBLIC fork — this must never be staged.
.codex/

# User-layer triage brief. doctor.mjs auto-copies it from modes/_brief.template.md,
# same as _profile.md / _custom.md above; tracking it would also orphan-flag in
# validate-system-paths-coverage.mjs.
modes/_brief.md

# Outreach drafts naming real people. Same reasoning as recruiter-outreach.md.
linkedin_post_reachout.md

# Report-workflow scratch: discarded reservations and stale-sentinel leftovers.
# reports/*.md is already ignored, but neither of these matches that pattern.
reports/.discarded/
reports/_stale_*

